/* ---------- GradeLanes: minimum water grade by process step (table block as "grades") ----------
   On a plate. Rows of the shared list grammar (index | step) with three lanes at the right, Potable, PW and WFI,
   drawn as single line-strong hairlines the full height of the list under plain lane labels. A flow line (the water
   path) runs from the step to its tap: a filled flow tap marks the minimum grade, an open tap an alternative. A step
   whose grade is "same as the product" gets a dashed open tap on every lane under a "= product" mark.
   Desktop: the step text is capped at 35rem and the lanes sit at the far right; the branch runs from the end of the
   text column across to its tap. */
.aq-grades { min-width: 0; }
.aq-grades__head, .aq-grades__row { display: grid; grid-template-columns: var(--space-12) minmax(0, 35rem) minmax(calc(var(--space-16) * 3), 1fr); column-gap: var(--space-6); }
